[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m # State Schema
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `state`: one of `CANDIDATE_SEARCH`, `CANDIDATE_SELECT`, or `DECISION`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `query`: the original user request. The harness does not parse it for you.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `allowed_tools`: valid tools for this turn.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `previous_searches`: previous `find_product` parameters. Do not repeat exact entries.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `failed_searches` / `failed_retry_searches`: previous `find_product` parameters that returned empty results. Do not repeat exact entries.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `last_errors`: structured errors from the latest failed tool/action attempt. Change the next action to fix them.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `candidate_pool`: search candidates as rows `[product_id, shop_id, title, price, service, sold_count]`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `previous_decision`: compact evidence from a prior checked selection after a retry.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `selected_products`: selected products as rows `[product_id, shop_id, title, price]`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `viewed_products`: product-detail evidence as rows `[product_id, title, price, shop_id, service, {"attrs": object, "sku_options": object, "detail": string}]`.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=97012)[0m - `budget_result`: deterministic result returned by `budget_check`.
